<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  A fragment of the Windows installer (MSI), named in tauri.bundle.conf.json (bundle.windows.wix).
  (It is called .wix.xml and not .wxs because Prettier takes .wxs for a script language and fails
  on it; the WiX compiler does not look at the extension.)

  The session daemon, norend.exe, sits next to noren.exe and is left running when the window of the
  app closes. Windows keeps the file of a running program open, so before the installer replaces or
  removes files it asks the daemon in the install folder to stop (norend.exe with its stop option: it ends its
  sessions, exits, and returns when its endpoint is free; nothing running there is not an error).

  The action is immediate, not deferred: it runs in the session of the person installing, with their
  token, which is the only one that can open the endpoint of their daemon (the pipe is closed to every
  other user, the system account included). It runs before InstallValidate, which is where Windows
  Installer looks for files in use. When the folder has no norend.exe yet (a first install) the
  action cannot start it, and that is ignored (Return="ignore").

  A fragment is linked only when something in it is referenced: the empty component group below is
  what tauri.bundle.conf.json references (bundle.windows.wix.componentGroupRefs), which brings the
  action and its place in the sequence along.
-->
<Wix xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/wix/2006/wi">
  <Fragment>
    <CustomAction
      Id="StopNorend"
      Directory="INSTALLDIR"
      ExeCommand="&quot;[INSTALLDIR]norend.exe&quot; --stop"
      Execute="immediate"
      Impersonate="yes"
      Return="ignore"
    />
    <InstallExecuteSequence>
      <Custom Action="StopNorend" Before="InstallValidate">1</Custom>
    </InstallExecuteSequence>
    <ComponentGroup Id="StopNorendGroup" />
  </Fragment>
</Wix>
